  "scope": "An isolated AARCH64 DarwinBoot EFI compiles/links with the exact Darwin22 608-byte command line and the production entropy helper. Before handoff the copied final ADT must contain one canonical /chosen and exactly one 256-byte random-seed. It is erased and filled by a fresh EFI_RNG_PROTOCOL RAW request; discovery, provider, zero-result and parser errors refuse handoff. Partial RNG errors and later loader failure erase the range. No time/CPU/build-seed fallback is installed. Fourteen provider/order, 408 malformed/truncation and three parameter cases run with ASan/UBSan/LSan, actual MdePkg headers and explicit RNG peers. The actual private iPhone ADT is accepted with a host RNG peer. Code/parser/EFI build evidence does not qualify the proprietary firmware provider, physical entropy/health, actual Boot/ExitBootServices execution, kernel consumption or phone boot. Existing firmware, payloads and images are unchanged."
